      "value": "@{62b61f8ec938a62475e4cd14|full_name}\n\nThere are two points.\n\nFirst, after creating instance with specifying a name for  a special purpose, it’s easy to forget to revert the name. In such cases, I think the instance name should be cleared by default. (Sorry—this Canny post didn’t mention the part about the last used name. It was originally part of my idea, but I lost track of it while writing.)\n\nSecond, as an option, using the username as the default for public instances is not ideal. There may not be an exact problem, but it could lead to misunderstandings—for example, making it looks like the instance has an “owner.”",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
